        "content": "<p>I have a definition that looks as follows:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">something</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And, I have defined different instances for <code>something A B</code>. But, when these two parameters are the same, I want to call it something else:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">special</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">something</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But unfortunately, none of the instance defined for <code>something A A</code> carries over to <code>special A</code>. How does one usually deal with such situation?</p>",
        "id": 621924983,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788624848
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>change <code>def</code> to <code>abbrev</code>?</p>",
        "id": 621925467,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1788625204
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, perfect. This fixed it. Thanks a lot!</p>",
        "id": 621925636,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788625290
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you don't plan to add more structure specific to <code>special</code>, you can also make <code>special</code> a notatation</p>",
        "id": 621925650,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1788625302
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Instances.20carrying.20over/near/621925650\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If you don't plan to add more structure specific to <code>special</code>, you can also make <code>special</code> a notatation</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I am not sure what you mean my more notations specific to <code>special</code>.<br>\nI have defined some instances just for <code>something A A</code>.</p>",
        "id": 621925858,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788625422
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One example in mathlib is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Module.End#doc\">docs#Module.End</a> . Because it carries new structure where it has composition as multiplication and algebra associated with it, it earned its status of being an <code>abbrev</code> instead of a mere notation</p>",
        "id": 621926295,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1788625683
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, cool.<br>\nFunnily enough, I am also working with <code>Hom</code> and <code>End</code> in my example <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span> <br>\nI just didn't want to type the whole thing out</p>",
        "id": 621926430,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788625777
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Instances.20carrying.20over/near/621926295\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it earned its status of being an <code>abbrev</code> instead of a mere notation</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Sounds like it should have earned its status of being a one-field <code>structure</code> instead of a mere <code>abbrev</code> <span aria-label=\"wink\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f609\" role=\"img\" title=\"wink\">:wink:</span></p>",
